INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261125-doj-speech-newsom-commutations', 'trump-justice-department-speech-newsom-death-row-commutations-blanche', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Trump uses a Justice Department speech to attack Newsom over California death row commutations', 'Speaking at the department on Monday, Nov. 23, the president called the clemency for more than 500 inmates a grave injustice. Newsom answered that he would not take lectures on accountability from Trump.', 'President Trump used a speech at the Justice Department on Monday, Nov. 23, to attack California Gov. Gavin Newsom over his decision to commute the death sentences of hundreds of inmates, the Associated Press reported.

Trump called the commutations one of the most shocking acts of injustice in the country''s history, according to the AP. Relatives of crime victims whose cases were affected by the clemency spoke during the event, and each criticized the governor''s decision.

## A partisan turn at the department

Attorney General Todd Blanche, Trump''s former personal defense lawyer, introduced the president and said the department was seeking the death penalty whenever appropriate, the AP reported. The AP described the address as Trump''s second at the Justice Department in under two years and said it turned partisan, with the president attacking Newsom and the Democratic Party as the "radical left."

Trump also credited his administration with a drop in violent crime. The AP noted that experts say crime has been falling since 2022.

## Newsom responds

Newsom said his decision in November to commute the sentences of more than 500 inmates to life without parole was among the hardest of his career, according to the AP. He said he would not take lectures on accountability from a president who has used the pardon power to help wealthy friends. Most of the commutations still need approval from the California Supreme Court, the AP reported.

## The political backdrop

The speech came after the November midterm elections gave Democrats control of both the House and the Senate. The AP reported that the new majorities could open congressional inquiries into Justice Department firings and into investigations of Trump''s adversaries.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Dept_of_Justice.jpg/1280px-Dept_of_Justice.jpg', 'The Robert F. Kennedy Department of Justice Building in Washington (file photo). Via Wikimedia Commons; editor to confirm the rights statement on the file page (photographer and license not yet confirmed)', 'licensed', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-25.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-25T11:00:00.000Z', '2026-11-25T11:00:00.000Z');
